      "judgment": {
        "status": "confirmed",
        "reasoning": "All 16 mathematical answers agree with their own captured worked solutions. q-73625 has pivots in columns 2, 3, and 4, hence rank 3. q-35734 reduces to pivots in columns 1, 2, and 3; its solution mistakenly names the matrix B instead of P, but the reduction and answer are correct. q-131302 has pivots in columns 1, 2, and 4 after exchanging the last two rows. For q-130256, yy' makes I nonlinear, while II and III are linear combinations of derivatives with coefficients depending only on x. Linearity gives 10 for q-64900 and x²−1 for q-79606. For q-181958, option 2 contains exactly (p,w), (q,w), (p,z), and (q,z), matching the completed source diagram despite different cropping. Cartesian-product cardinalities are 10·10=100 and 7·6=42. The homogeneous equations give Ae^(−6x) and Ae^(5x). Substituting y_p=x²/2−x gives 2y_p'+2y_p=x²−2. The probability answers follow respectively from the indicated cell, summing three disjoint cells, summing four cells in the union without double counting, and summing the X=2 row. No submitted grades or earlier answers were supplied; confirmation rests on the captured worked solutions.",
